      {
        "id": 181625,
        "name": "Bowie",
        "username": "Bowie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bowie/{size}/2097_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-08-25T12:23:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Heroes are one card each variant. There are (currently) 180* hero variants [including their standard versions].<br>Villains are two cards each variant or one oversized card. There are (currently) 61 villain cards and 31 oversized cards, the weird math being Operative's fault.<br>Hero decks are 40 cards. There are (currently) 26 heroes.<br>Vengeance decks are 20 cards and one oversized card. There are 15 vengeance villains with 15 oversized cards.<br>Villain decks are 25 cards. There are (currently) 24 standard villains.<br>Environment decks are 15 cards. There are (currently) 22 environments.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br><br>This is, at the moment, 2,511 standard cards and 46 oversized cards.</p>\n<p>*This includes all variants in existence, which is complicated by the foil set, because it includes heroes there are no decks for yet.<br>\nThis includes the Sentinels being 4 for each variant, and Sky-Scraper being 3 for each variant.<br>\nAnd while this does include foil reprints of previous cards, THIS DOES NOT INCLUDE non-foil versions of promos we haven’t seen yet. (e.g. the Freedom Five promos, Setting Sun Ra, et cetera.)</p>\n<p>Ultimately, after we get OblivAeon and thus the non-foil versions of new cards, there will be 220 hero cards total, including the decks we haven’t seen yet.<br>\nThere will be effectively three new villain decks with one currently unsleevable villain card and a deck of oversized villain cards (vengeance style). I’ll wait to do the math for that but I can make guesses (75 deck cards, maybe 15 oversized?) on OblivAeon’s stuff until playtesting is done.<br>\nWe have 2 new environment decks coming, for another 30 cards.<br>\nWe have 11 new hero decks coming, for 440 deck cards more to come.</p>\n<p>So all in total, that’s another 585 or so standard cards, plus another 15 or so oversized cards. So you’re looking at ~3,100.00 standard cards, and ~61 oversized cards.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:06:25.471Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
